# modules/ mixes BOARD-AUTHORED sources (tracked, un-ignored below) with copies
# staged at build time from runtime/ and the files build.sh generates. The
# staged half is build output -- edit runtime/ instead -- and without an ignore
# rule it sits in `git status` forever and a `git add -A` commits it.
#
# A PATTERN, not a list. Until #161 Phase 3 this file enumerated every staged
# module by name, which was a second copy of build.sh's staging allowlist (and
# the repo root's .gitignore held a third). It had gone stale in both
# directions: it still named canvas.py, palette.py, web_view.py and
# web_view_page.py, none of which are staged any more, and any module added to
# runtime/ would have had to be added here too. Staging is a DENYLIST now
# (board.toml), so a new shared module reaches the board with nobody editing
# anything -- and an ignore rule that had to be edited per module would have
# handed the paperwork straight back.
#
# Un-ignore a new board-authored file explicitly, as the entries below do.
modules/*
!modules/boot.py
!modules/main.py
!modules/moybyte_shell.py
!modules/moybyte_sd.py
!modules/moybyte_diag.py
!modules/moy_runtime.py
!modules/moy_canvas.py
!modules/moy_compositor.py
!modules/moy_ota.py
!modules/moy_webserver.py
!modules/moy_webhost.py
!modules/moycore_glue.py
!modules/tdeck_board.py
!modules/tdeck_display.py
!modules/device_api.py
!modules/device_audio.py
!modules/device_canvas.py
!modules/device_diag.py
!modules/device_input.py
!modules/device_util.py
!modules/device_wifi.py
# The moybyte PACKAGE (moybyte.input -- the boards' InputState + the T-Deck
# keyboard matrix). The DIRECTORY has to be un-ignored: git does not descend
# into an ignored directory, so a rule naming files inside it would never be
# consulted.
!modules/moybyte/

# Toolchain + build tree (contains nested git repos).
.build/
dist/
